API_KEY=your-key       # Free stock footage and images\n234: UNSPLASH_ACCESS_KEY=your-key   # Free stock images\n235: \n236: # Music:\n237: SUNO_API_KEY=your-key          # Full songs, instrumentals, any genre\n238: \n239: # Voice & images:\n240: ELEVENLABS_API_KEY=your-key    # Premium TTS, AI music, sound effects\n241: OPENAI_API_KEY=your-key        # OpenAI TTS, GPT Image 2 images\n242: XAI_API_KEY=your-key           # xAI Grok image edits/generation + Grok video generation\n243: GOOGLE_API_KEY=your-key        # Google Imagen images, Google TTS (700+ voices)\n244: \n245: # More video providers:\n246: HEYGEN_API_KEY=your-key        # HeyGen — VEO, Sora, Runway, Kling via single gateway\n247: RUNWAY_API_KEY=your-key        # Runway Gen-4 direct\n248: ```\n249: \n250: <details>\n251: <summary><strong>Have a GPU? Unlock free local video generation</strong></summary>\n252: \n253: ```bash\n254: make install-gpu\n255: \n256: # Then add to .env:\n257: VIDEO_GEN_LOCAL_ENABLED=true\n258: VIDEO_GEN_LOCAL_MODEL=wan2.1-1.3b  # or wan2.1-14b, hunyuan-1.5, ltx2-local, cogvideo-5b\n259: ```\n260: \n261: </details>\n262: \n263: ---\n264: \n265: ## What You Get With Zero API Keys\n266: \n267: You don't need paid API keys to make real videos. Out of the box, `make setup` gives you:\n268: \n269: | Capability | Free Tool | What It Does |\n270: |-----------|-----------|-------------|\n271: | **Narration** | Piper TTS | Free offline text-to-speech — real human-sounding narration |\n272: | **Open footage** | Archive.org + NASA + Wikimedia Commons | Free/open archival footage, educational media, and documentary texture |\n273: | **Extra stock** | Pexels + Unsplash + Pixabay | Free stock footage/images (developer keys are free to get) |\n274: | **Composition (React)** | Remotion | React-based rendering — spring-animated image scenes, text cards, stat cards, charts, TikTok-style word-level captions, TalkingHead |\n275: | **Composition (HTML/GSAP)** | HyperFrames | HTML/CSS/GSAP rendering — kinetic typography, product promos, launch reels, registry blocks, website-to-video, rigged SVG character animation |\n276: | **Post-production** | FFmpeg | Encoding, subtitle burn-in, audio mixing, color grading |\n277: | **Subtitles** | Built-in | Auto-generated captions with word-level timing |\n278: \n279: OpenMontage picks between Remotion and HyperFrames at proposal time (locked as `render_runtime`). Remotion is the default for data-driven explainers and anything using the existing React scene stack; HyperFrames is the default for motion-graphics-heavy briefs that express naturally as HTML + GSAP, including the `character-animation` pipeline's SVG/GSAP rig output. See `skills/core/hyperframes.md` for the full decision matrix.\n280: \n281: **Two free-ish paths:**\n282: \n283: - **Image-based video:** Piper narrates your script, images provide the visuals, and Remotion animates them into a polished edit.\n284: - **Local character animation:** SVG rigs, pose libraries, GSAP timelines, and HyperFrames render cartoon character acting to `projects/<project-name>/renders/final.mp4`.\n285: - **Real-footage video:** the documentary montage pipeline builds a CLIP-searchable corpus from Archive.org, NASA, Wikimedia Commons, and optional free-key sources like Pexels and Unsplash, then cuts together actual motion footage into a finished video.\n286: \n287: If you want the second one, prompt for a **documentary montage**, **tone poem**, or **stock-footage collage**, and explicitly say **use real footage only**.\n288: \n289: ---\n290: \n291: ## Try These Prompts\n292: \n293: Copy any of these into your AI coding assistant after setup. Each one runs a full production pipeline.\n294: \n295: ### Start from a reference video\n296: \n297: > \"Here's a YouTube short I love. Make me something like this, but about CRISPR for high school students.\"\n298: \n299: > \"Analyze this Reel and give me 3 original variants I could make for my own product launch.\"\n300: \nThe above content does NOT show the entire file contents. If you need to view any lines of the file which were not shown to complete your task, call this tool again to view those lines.\n"}
