{"step_index":45,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-23T16:53:57Z","content":"Created At: 2026-08-23T22:23:57+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-08-23T22:23:57+05:30\nFile Path: `file:///C:/Users/renu5/Downloads/find-skill-repo/all%20github%20repos/claude-seo/README.md`\nTotal Lines: 491\nTotal Bytes: 37991\nShowing lines 1 to 150\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: ![Claude SEO cover: a Claude Code command palette with /seo audit, schema, geo, content, and backlinks commands over a dark CRT panel](assets/cover.svg)\r\n2: \r\n3: # Claude SEO: SEO Skill for Claude Code\r\n4: \r\n5: **Claude SEO is an open-source SEO analysis plugin for [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/claude-code).** It runs 25 sub-skills and 18 specialist agents in parallel across technical SEO, content quality (E-E-A-T), Schema.org markup, AI search optimization (GEO), local SEO, e-commerce, and international SEO. Every audit produces a prioritized action plan with testable recommendations grounded in primary-source guidance from Google.\r\n6: \r\n7: [![CI](https://github.com/AgriciDaniel/claude-seo/actions/workflows/ci.yml/badge.svg)](https://github.com/AgriciDaniel/claude-seo/actions/workflows/ci.yml)\r\n8: [![Claude Code Skill](https://img.shields.io/badge/Claude%20Code-Skill-blue)](https://claude.ai/claude-code)\r\n9: [![License: MIT](https://img.shields.io/badge/License-MIT-yellow.svg)](LICENSE)\r\n10: [![Version](https://img.shields.io/github/v/release/AgriciDaniel/claude-seo)](https://github.com/AgriciDaniel/claude-seo/releases)\r\n11: [![Tests](https://img.shields.io/badge/tests-326%20passing-brightgreen)](tests/)\r\n12: [![Community](https://img.shields.io/badge/AI%20Marketing%20Hub-Pro%20community-purple)](https://www.skool.com/ai-marketing-hub-pro)\r\n13: \r\n14: > **Two versions of this skill.**\r\n15: > - 🌐 **Public open-source** → [`AgriciDaniel/claude-seo`](https://github.com/AgriciDaniel/claude-seo): MIT, public releases, no membership. Use this if you want stable + downloadable.\r\n16: > - 🔒 **Community private mirror** → [`AI-Marketing-Hub/claude-seo`](https://github.com/AI-Marketing-Hub/claude-seo): early access to upcoming features and direct collaboration with the [AI Marketing Hub Pro](https://www.skool.com/ai-marketing-hub-pro) community. Requires membership.\r\n17: \r\n18: ### Why Claude SEO\r\n19: \r\n20: - **AI-search first.** Aligned with [Google's AI Optimization Guide](https://developers.google.com/search/docs/fundamentals/ai-optimization-guide). Question-based citability scoring, primary-source evidence on llms.txt, IPTC `TrainedAlgorithmicMedia` for AI-generated product images, agent-friendly page checks per [web.dev](https://web.dev/).\r\n21: - **Parallel execution.** Full site audits spawn up to 15 specialist agents simultaneously. Site-level audits complete in minutes rather than hours.\r\n22: - **Falsifiable, not promotional.** Every recommendation carries the first-principle observation it rests on, its dependency relationships, an explicit \"how would we know this failed?\" check, and a leading indicator. See [Methodology](#methodology).\r\n23: \r\n24: ### Real results\r\n25: \r\n26: ![Google Search Console clicks and impressions for a three-month-old site climbing from launch to steady organic growth between 23 March and 12 June 2026](assets/growth-3-months.png)\r\n27: \r\n28: Google Search Console for a site started 23 March 2026 and run on this workflow: total clicks and impressions across its first three months, through 12 June 2026.\r\n29: \r\n30: > Using Codex instead of Claude Code? Use [Codex SEO](https://github.com/AgriciDaniel/codex-seo), the Codex-first port with TOML agents, plugin packaging, deterministic runners, and the same SEO workflow surface.\r\n31: \r\n32: ## Who this is for\r\n33: \r\n34: - **SEO agencies running 5+ client sites.** Replace quarterly deep audits with weekly automated runs. Same team capacity, 4× audit cadence, every recommendation comes with a falsifiability check the client can verify.\r\n35: - **In-house SEO leads at SaaS / publisher / e-commerce companies.** Second-pair-of-eyes before executive reviews. Catches what GSC and Lighthouse hide: schema deprecation, AI-citability gaps, expired-domain heritage risk, parasite-SEO exposure, machine-translation drift.\r\n36: - **Freelance SEO consultants.** Anchor day-one client scope with a 15-minute audit and a real 0-100 score. Win the engagement with concrete proof of value before you spend an hour writing the proposal.\r\n37: \r\n38: ![Claude SEO /seo command demo in Claude Code terminal](screenshots/seo-command-demo.gif)\r\n39: \r\n40: Run a full audit and watch parallel agents fan out across the site:\r\n41: \r\n42: ![Claude SEO /seo audit demo: parallel subagents producing a prioritized action plan](screenshots/seo-audit-demo.gif)\r\n43: \r\n44: [Watch the full demo on YouTube](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=COMnNlUakQk)\r\n45: \r\n46: ## Table of Contents\r\n47: \r\n48: - [Who this is for](#who-this-is-for)\r\n49: - [Installation](#installation)\r\n50: - [Quick Start](#quick-start)\r\n51: - [Commands](#commands)\r\n52: - [Features](#features)\r\n53: - [Compared to manual / agency / commercial tools](#compared-to-manual--agency--commercial-tools)\r\n54: - [Use cases](#use-cases)\r\n55: - [Sample Output](#sample-output)\r\n56: - [Architecture](#architecture)\r\n57: - [Methodology](#methodology)\r\n58: - [What's New in v2](#whats-new-in-v2)\r\n59: - [Limitations](#limitations)\r\n60: - [Requirements](#requirements)\r\n61: - [Uninstall](#uninstall)\r\n62: - [Extensions](#extensions)\r\n63: - [Ecosystem](#ecosystem)\r\n64: - [Documentation](#documentation)\r\n65: - [FAQ](#faq)\r\n66: - [Community Contributors](#community-contributors)\r\n67: - [License](#license)\r\n68: - [Contributing](#contributing)\r\n69: - [Author](#author)\r\n70: \r\n71: ## Installation\r\n72: \r\n73: > ℹ️ **Which version are you installing?**\r\n74: >\r\n75: > - **Public open-source (default).** The commands below install from [`AgriciDaniel/claude-seo`](https://github.com/AgriciDaniel/claude-seo) — MIT, public releases, no membership required.\r\n76: > - **AI Marketing Hub Pro member?** Install the community version with early access instead: swap `AgriciDaniel/claude-seo` for `AI-Marketing-Hub/claude-seo` and the plugin slug `claude-seo@agricidaniel-claude-seo` for `claude-seo@ai-marketing-hub-claude-seo`. Requires `gh auth login` (or PAT) with access to the `AI-Marketing-Hub` org. If `/plugin marketplace add` 404s, DM in the [Skool community](https://www.skool.com/ai-marketing-hub-pro) to get added.\r\n77: \r\n78: ### Plugin Install (Claude Code 1.0.33+)\r\n79: \r\n80: The fastest path. One-time marketplace add, then plugin install:\r\n81: \r\n82: ```bash\r\n83: /plugin marketplace add AgriciDaniel/claude-seo\r\n84: /plugin install claude-seo@agricidaniel-claude-seo\r\n85: ```\r\n86: \r\n87: ### Manual Install (Unix / macOS / Linux)\r\n88: \r\n89: ```bash\r\n90: git clone --depth 1 https://github.com/AgriciDaniel/claude-seo.git\r\n91: bash claude-seo/install.sh\r\n92: ```\r\n93: \r\n94: <details>\r\n95: <summary>One-liner (curl, review then run)</summary>\r\n96: \r\n97: ```bash\r\n98: curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/AgriciDaniel/claude-seo/main/install.sh > install.sh\r\n99: cat install.sh        # review before running\r\n100: bash install.sh\r\n101: rm install.sh\r\n102: ```\r\n103: \r\n104: </details>\r\n105: \r\n106: ### Windows (PowerShell)\r\n107: \r\n108: ```powershell\r\n109: git clone --depth 1 https://github.com/AgriciDaniel/claude-seo.git\r\n110: powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File claude-seo\\install.ps1\r\n111: ```\r\n112: \r\n113: > **Why `git clone` instead of `irm | iex`?** Claude Code's own security guardrails flag `irm ... | iex` as a supply chain risk: downloading and executing remote code without verification. The `git clone` approach lets you inspect `claude-seo\\install.ps1` before running it.\r\n114: \r\n115: ## Quick Start\r\n116: \r\n117: ```bash\r\n118: # Start Claude Code\r\n119: claude\r\n120: \r\n121: # Full site audit: parallel sub-agents produce a prioritized action plan\r\n122: /seo audit https://example.com\r\n123: \r\n124: # Deep single-page analysis: on-page elements, content quality, schema\r\n125: /seo page https://example.com/about\r\n126: \r\n127: # Schema markup audit: detect, validate, generate\r\n128: /seo schema https://example.com\r\n129: \r\n130: # AI search optimization: passage citability + primary-source-aligned recommendations\r\n131: /seo geo https://example.com\r\n132: \r\n133: # Generate a sitemap with industry templates\r\n134: /seo sitemap generate\r\n135: ```\r\n136: \r\n137: ## Commands\r\n138: \r\n139: ![Claude SEO sub-skill ecosystem: 25 modules grouped into 8 categories (audit, content, schema, technical, AI search, local + maps, commerce + intl, extensions) around the central orchestrator](assets/sub-skills.svg)\r\n140: \r\n141: 25 user-invocable `/seo` commands across the orchestrator and its sub-skills. Full reference in [docs/COMMANDS.md](docs/COMMANDS.md).\r\n142: \r\n143: | Command | Description |\r\n144: |---------|-------------|\r\n145: | `/seo audit <url>` | Full website audit with parallel sub-agent delegation |\r\n146: | `/seo page <url>` | Deep single-page analysis |\r\n147: | `/seo technical <url>` | Technical SEO audit across 9 categories |\r\n148: | `/seo content <url>` | E-E-A-T and content quality analysis |\r\n149: | `/seo content-brief <topic>` | Detailed content brief: target keywords, outline, internal links |\r\n150: | `/seo schema <url>` | Detect, validate, and generate Schema.org markup |\r\nThe above content does NOT show the entire file contents. If you need to view any lines of the file which were not shown to complete your task, call this tool again to view those lines.\n"}
